{
  "_comment": "Streamline seeding config. Seeds are scattered directly on the car's surface (snapped to the real baked occupancy grid, then offset outward along its normal), one 'group' (component region) at a time, then traced in BOTH directions to find the upstream origin and downstream exit -- see src/particles/seeding.js and streamlines.js's traceBidirectional. Not baked, hand-authored; lives alongside occupancy_grid.* because both are fetched at runtime the same way. Region coordinates are fractions of the car's own dimensions (see src/particles/anchors.js): alongFlow is a fraction of domain.halfLength from the car's centre (-1 = front-most extent, +1 = rear-most extent); lateral is a fraction of the car's own half-width from the centreline; vertical is a fraction of the car's own height above the ground. A region is a [min,max] RANGE on each axis -- a rough box around the component, not a tight fit to its actual (often curved) surface. `mirror: true` doubles a group onto the opposite side of the centreline (count applies PER SIDE). `count` is the target LINE COUNT for that group. Phase 3.7: counts raised from a ~138-line total toward the 400-600 visual target (the author's explicit ask) -- group regions/positions unchanged from Phase 3.6, only counts scaled. Later Phase 3.7 addendum: `nose` widened (lateral/vertical/alongFlow) and `cockpit`/`chassis` (new) added so the front-wing/nose-flank/nose-pillar/cockpit-surround/chassis-flank guide curves below have real surface seeds to act on -- see PROGRESS.md.",
  "seeding": {
    "lineCountCap": 400,
    "candidateMultiplier": 6,
    "minSeparationWorld": 0.03,
    "maxSurfaceDistanceCells": 3,
    "surfaceOffsetCells": 1.6
  },
  "_comment_zigzagFix": "Addendum: three knobs added to fix visible zigzag/clutter on tight-hugging lines, all with defaults matching their code-side CONFIG objects (kept here too so they're tunable without touching code, same as `seeding` above). fieldRepulsion (src/particles/vectorField.js FIELD_REPULSION_CONFIG): a soft push away from the nearest occupied surface baked into the field itself, fading to zero by radiusCells grid cells out, so the hard SDF clamp in streamlines.js rarely needs to fire at all. smoothing (streamlines.js SMOOTHING_CONFIG): Laplacian smoothing of each traced polyline after tracing to remove residual sawtooth from whatever clamp firings still happen, with a re-check-and-reclamp against the real grid afterward since smoothing can push a point back into geometry. culling (streamlines.js CULL_CONFIG): drops lines that never stray far from freestream anywhere along their length ('uninteresting') or that needed the hard clamp more than maxClampFireCount times ('misbehaving'), then tops back up with replacement seeds so culling doesn't thin the overall picture below lineCountCap.",
  "fieldRepulsion": {
    "enabled": true,
    "radiusCells": 3,
    "strengthFraction": 1
  },
  "smoothing": {
    "enabled": true,
    "maxSegmentWorld": 0.005,
    "subdivideWithinCells": 2.5,
    "finalStandoffCells": 0.5,
    "rounds": 3,
    "passes": 4,
    "alpha": 0.5
  },
  "culling": {
    "enabled": true,
    "minMaxDeviationFraction": 0.15,
    "maxClampFireCount": 100,
    "maxTopUpRounds": 14,
    "maxTurnDegrees": 30,
    "maxSeedOffsetCells": 3.2,
    "seedOffsetStepCells": 0.4
  },
