  "_primitivesComment": "Phase 3.7: doublets REMOVED entirely (they couldn't represent thin multi-element geometry like the front wing, and produced closed recirculation loops -- see PHASE-3.7.md's intro and src/particles/primitives.js). What remains: vortex filaments at the wing tips and diffuser edges (kept per section 4 -- they produce trailing spiral structure guide curves alone don't), and the sidepod sinks / diffuser source, now at LOW strength (halved from the Phase 3.6 values) since guide curves do the routing work now and these are meant as texture, not the primary pull. `decayLength` stays ~5.2 (a car length). Their swirl/pull is capped by flowInvariant.js's global lateral+vertical limit applied to the FINAL field in vectorField.js, so none of them can close a loop on their own regardless of strength.",
